From 3a2839dd00efad65e6876abec149dfae62c4c7a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 09:48:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] www: Wireless Log - your device names, each network's type,
 the main network wherever it sits (102.8 line)

Field report (GT-BE98, v3.6.2).
- Names: httpd sends only the DHCP lease hostname (what the device reported, "*" when nothing);
  the stock page put the client list's name over an empty or "*" one and this page had dropped
  that. nameOf(): your name (custom_clientlist, then the live list; by MAC, then IP) first, the
  lease hostname after.
- Network types: every box but the main one carried a "Guest Network" chip, so main + guest + IoT
  read as two guest networks. A box is labelled with its Guest Network Pro type (sdn_rl +
  apg<idx>_ssid -> the stock labels).
- Layout: the page assumed the main network on wlN.1 (a MAINFH profile). A box without MAINFH rows
  keeps the main network on the primary wlN and the others from wlN.1: there the guest was titled
  as the main network and the main network's clients were filed under the backhaul. The layout now
  follows sdn_rl; the radio's BSSID goes to the box whose SSID it carries.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/www/Reaper_WLog.asp | 87 +++++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 73 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/release/src/router/www/Reaper_WLog.asp b/release/src/router/www/Reaper_WLog.asp
index 308f4ab7b91..2a123bc0f68 100644
--- a/release/src/router/www/Reaper_WLog.asp
+++ b/release/src/router/www/Reaper_WLog.asp
@@ -21,7 +21,13 @@
      2026-10-26: one box per network inside each radio (testers read one mixed table as one network). On this
      firmware the primary BSS wlN is the hidden AiMesh backhaul carrier, wlN.1 the main network (its clients carry
      ""), wlN.2 / wlN.3 the guests; the main box is titled with wlN.1_ssid. With wlN.1 off the primary is the main
-     network. In AP mode the radio's SSID / BSSID (dataarray, read from wlN) belong to whichever box they name. -->
+     network. In AP mode the radio's SSID / BSSID (dataarray, read from wlN) belong to whichever box they name.
+     2026-10-30: a box other than the main network is labelled with its Guest Network Pro type (Guest, IoT, Kids,
+     VPN ...) - every one was called a guest network; names are your device names first, the lease hostname after.
+     2026-10-30 (field, GT-BE98): the layout above holds once the main network is a Guest Network Pro MAINFH profile
+     (sdn_rl carries MAINFH rows). A box without them keeps the main network on the primary wlN (named by wlN_ssid)
+     and its other networks from wlN.1 up - there the page had titled the guest network as the main one, called the
+     next network a guest and filed the main network's clients under the backhaul. -->
